---
/* THE MARK IS NOT IN THIS ROW. It stands on the ASCII band directly above,
   which is where the page closes; what is left here is one thin row, and it
   is thin on purpose: a footer that has to be scrolled through is a footer
   that has been given something to say.

   TWO GROUPS, AND THE SIDE EACH ONE SITS ON IS WHAT IT IS FOR. Left is the
   project and the house it is built in -- licence, source, room, SW labs,
   LinkedIn. Right is what the law wants. A reader looking for either knows
   which half to look at without reading the other.

   The address is gone from here on purpose. It is the one thing in this row
   that would ask to be acted on, and the section above is where the page asks
   for that action -- an address in both places is the reader deciding which of
   the two is the real one.

   THE LEGAL LINKS ARE THREE AND THEY RESOLVE. They were four and they
   resolved to nothing: the row was drawn ahead of the pages so that the day
   the pages landed nothing here had to be found and rewired, which is what
   happened. Imprint, Privacy and Terms are written; DPA is gone, and the
   reason it is gone is in ../lib/legal beside the list itself, because a
   removed link is exactly the kind of decision that gets quietly re-added.

   THE ROW IS NOT A LIST TYPED HERE. It comes off `LEGAL_ROUTES`, which the
   pages themselves do not read -- their routes are their filenames -- so this
   is still the one place that decides what the footer offers. What it buys is
   that the deploy check can walk the same list and refuse a build where one of
   them is missing.

   SW LABS IS `sw-labs.de`, NOT `.com`. The brief said `.com`; the canonical
   URL in the SW labs site's own head, the CMS and deck subdomains, and the
   address in the section above are all `.de`. */
import { LICENCE } from '../lib/osMarks';
import { LINKS } from '../lib/linkMarks';
import { LEGAL_ROUTES } from '../lib/legal';
---
<footer class="foot">
  <div class="wrap foot__in">
    <nav class="foot__meta mono" aria-label="Project">
      {/* The same mark the hero's fact strip carries, at the same size. The
          licence is named twice on this page and it is a mark both times. */}
      <span class="foot__lic">
        <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d={LICENCE.path} /></svg>
        {LICENCE.label}
      </span>
      {/* FOUR LINKS, EACH WITH A MARK, AND THE ORDER IS NEAREST-TO-THE-CODE
          FIRST: where it is written, where it is talked about, where the house
          is, where the house posts.

          THE HOUSE'S PAGE IS IN THE LEFT GROUP because this half of the row is
          the project and the house it is built in, and LinkedIn is where the
          house is.

          THERE IS NO X AND THERE WILL NOT BE ONE. The account exists and it
          belongs to the maintainer rather than to SW labs, so a link here
          would point a reader looking for the company at a person.

          Three of the four marks are the vendor's own, licensed rather than
          copied, and the fourth is a globe because SW labs has no mark to
          license -- ../lib/linkMarks carries why, including why the whole row
          moved onto one package to get LinkedIn's real mark.

          Each keeps its own viewBox: they are all 16 today, and a row drawn on
          a number typed here would be wrong the day one of them is not. */}
      {LINKS.map((l) => (
        <a class="foot__l" href={l.href}>
          <svg class="mark" viewBox={l.viewBox} aria-hidden="true"><path d={l.path} /></svg>
          {l.label}
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <nav class="foot__legal mono" aria-label="Legal">
      {LEGAL_ROUTES.map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}
    </nav>
  </div>
</footer>
